ra system  just like the s20 ultra it has 10 on the  front which is weird it's a little bit  less than 4k so they're up sampling it  and we have that super zoom camera the  iphone is limited to 10 times  zoom so here's a comparison between the  two at 10 times  of course the iphone also has the deep  fusion text so let me know which one of  these  looks better here's a series of images  you guys take a look and let me know  what looks best  we're going to be doing a detailed  unbiased  blind comparison between these two those  are always so much fun to shoot  and to record for you guys so make sure  you guys have those notifications  enabled  to get a true detailed sense of how  these two stack up  before i give you guys my final  conclusion there are two unique features  with both of these phones that i have to  mention  the iphone has the apple ecosystem  behind it works great with my macbooks  works great with my apple watch  people love it they're stuck in that  system and that's a definite plus even  if it has a lot of other downfalls  the note 20 it has the s pen now i have  to be honest  i usually only use this for the first  maybe a week or so and then i end up  using my notes  like regular phones i've done that ever  since the original note  a lot of people love this though if  you're somebody that wants to draw  you want to write this thing is  excellent having that capability and  samsung has now updated this  with extremely little lag this matches  up to the  uh basically the ipad pro now with this  120 hertz screen you guys could see  compared to the samsung tablets this is  way better  at least until that s7 plus comes out  and it will match up with this but if  you're somebody  that can appreciate the s pen that is  definitely a huge  bonus now let's get into the final  conclusion  what do i think about these two phones  well  if you're not stuck in the apple  ecosystem i really like the note i love  the way it looks i love the way it feels  i love th